#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""shell-health: is every background job on this laptop still working?

  shell-health [--json]     {"worst": "ok|stale|failed", "jobs": [...]}   (default)
  shell-health --text       a readable table
  shell-health --only ID    just that job (ids: see --text)
  shell-health --refresh    also ask updates-check to look again now (otherwise its cache is used)

Each job: {id, name, state, since, why, unit, log, run}
  state  ok | healing | stale | failed | off
         off = the unit does not exist here; left out of "worst"
         healing = not proven working, but already on its way back and inside its grace: a timer job
         that has not run since the laptop started or woke (counted from then, not from the last
         success), a run that failed once below the job's own threshold with the retry scheduled,
         a service starting or restarting, a network job while offline, a network job whose failures
         all came in the 5 minutes since a wake (the network coming back), Microsoft 365 down only
         since such a wake.  why says what it is waiting
         for and when the next try is due.  Left out of "worst"; it turns stale or failed when the
         grace runs out.
  since  ISO time of the last success ("" when unknown)
  why    one short plain sentence
  log    shell command that shows the job's log;  run  shell command that runs it now ("")

Guards against false alarms (2026-11-20; `health-report` shows how noisy the pill has been):
  confirm   a job is raised (stale/failed) only once it has not been ok for CONFIRM (100 s, two
            polls); until then it is healing, "checking again".  Time already spent healing
            counts, so a grace that ends in a real failure is raised at once.
  online    means usable: a default route AND NetworkManager connectivity not none/portal/limited
            (a wake has a route before DNS; campus Wi-Fi has a portal).  nmcli unsure: the route.
  wake      every network job that went bad only since the last wake (WAKE_SLACK early) is
            healing for WAKE_GRACE; timer jobs with a streak file and Microsoft date their own
            failures and do this themselves.
  unknown   a probe that timed out (systemd, Docker, gsettings) keeps the job's last known state
            and says "could not check just now"; it never turns a job off or green.
  restarts  counted over the last hour (history in seen.json), not over the unit's lifetime.
  units     any other failed user unit is amber, not red (fumon has already announced it), after
            the same confirmation; IGNORE_UNITS and health.json "ignoreUnits" (globs) leave it out.
  repairs   a job's script may fix things itself (pull-mail restarts a stuck DavMail); the stamp
            file is shown in why for 6 h ("restarted DavMail itself 10 min ago, which fixed it").

"stale" means a timer job whose last success is older than about three times its period
(a floor for the fast ones; weekly jobs are stale after two periods and a day), counted from the
last start or wake when that is later.  A job that
reports its own failures is failed from the same count its own watcher uses.  Offline, the
network jobs get a grace period before they count (why says "offline").

Notices.  Besides jobs there is a second kind of row, {state: "notice", kind: "notice"}, for things
worth knowing that are not failures: pending updates, firmware, a restart, low disk space.  They
never affect "worst".  Extra keys: group (updates|firmware|reboot|disk), count, detail, cmd (what
the person would run; never run from here), actionable (true for security updates, more than
`updatesNag` packages, lists older than `staleListDays`, a pending restart, low disk), say (true
for the two the island may announce: low disk and restart needed).  The top level also has
"attention" (how many are actionable) and "hidden" ([{id, name}] of what the person stopped watching).
Updates come from updates-check --cached (never waits; it refreshes its own cache in the
background at most every 6 hours).  Disk rows use os.statvfs on the real mounted filesystems
(by fstype: no tmpfs, squashfs, FUSE, network or container mounts).

Settings: ~/.config/shell/health.json (all keys optional)
  {"updatesNag": 50, "staleListDays": 14, "diskPercent": 10, "diskGB": 5, "espMB": 20,
   "hidden": ["calibre-backup"], "ignoreUnits": ["some-flaky@*.service"], "notices": {"updates": true, "firmware": true, "disk": true, "reboot": true}}
A job or notice id in "hidden" is left out of jobs and worst altogether.

Read-only: it reads systemd's state, the streak files the sync scripts leave under
$XDG_STATE_HOME, backup folders, gsettings, findmnt, nmcli, docker inspect and stat -f on the music card.  It never lists or reads inside the
Box mount.  Its only write is $XDG_STATE_HOME/shell-health/seen.json (when each job was last
seen working, and since when the network has been down).  Every subprocess has a timeout;
the whole run is bounded by about 3 seconds.

Test hooks (environment): SHELL_HEALTH_NOW (epoch), SHELL_HEALTH_ROUTE (stand-in for
/proc/net/route), SHELL_HEALTH_NETDIR (stand-in for /proc/net), HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME,
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, PATH, SHELL_HEALTH_CONFIG (stand-in for health.json),
SHELL_HEALTH_WAKE (epoch of the last start or wake, in place of /proc/stat btime and
the journal; empty reads them), SHELL_HEALTH_PROCSTAT (stand-in for /proc/stat), SHELL_HEALTH_DISKS (a JSON file {mountpoint: {fstype, total, free}} in place of /proc/self/mountinfo
and statvfs), SHELL_HEALTH_UPDATES (the updates-check program; "none" for no notices), SHELL_HEALTH_CONFIRM
(seconds; 0 turns confirmation off), SHELL_HEALTH_CONNECTIVITY (in place of nmcli's answer),
SHELL_HEALTH_ARCHIVE_DEV and SHELL_HEALTH_ARCHIVE_DIR (the music card's device and mount point).
"""
import concurrent.futures as cf
import datetime
import fnmatch
import json
import os
import subprocess
import sys
import time

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
STATE = os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or os.path.join(HOME, ".local/state")
RUNTIME = os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") or "/run/user/%d" % os.getuid()
NOW = float(os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_NOW") or time.time())
GRACE = 30 * 60               # offline this long before a network job counts as bad
WAKE_GRACE = 5 * 60           # a network job's failures this soon after a wake are the network coming back
WAKE_SLACK = 60               # the journal logs the wake a few seconds after resumed jobs already ran
# A job turns stale or failed only once it has looked bad this long (two polls of the pill, which runs
# this every 2 min); until then it is healing, "checking again".  Of the alerts between 2026-11-15
# and 11-20, 7 in 10 cleared on their own within 2-4 minutes.
CONFIRM = float(os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_CONFIRM") or 100)
RESTART_WINDOW = 3600   # restarts counted over the last hour, not since the unit started
RESTARTS_STALE = 3                       # this many in the window: stale
SEEN = {}                                # seen.json, loaded before the judges run (restart history)
MIN, H, D = 60, 3600, 86400
SYSCTL = ["systemctl", "--user"]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- small helpers
def run(argv, env=None, timeout=1.8):
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env)
        return p.returncode, p.stdout
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return 124, ""                   # did not answer in time: unknown, not absent
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return 255, ""


def read(path, default=""):
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return f.read()
    except OSError:
        return default


def mtime(path):
    try:
        return os.stat(path).st_mtime
    except OSError:
        return 0.0


def iso(ts):
    if not ts:
        return ""
    return datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(ts).astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds")


def ago(sec):
    sec = max(0, int(sec))
    if sec < 90:
        return "just now"
    if sec < 90 * MIN:
        return "%d min ago" % round(sec / MIN)
    if sec < 36 * H:
        return "%d h ago" % round(sec / H)
    return "%d days ago" % round(sec / D)


def span(sec):
    return ago(sec).replace(" ago", "").replace("just now", "a moment")


def ts_of(v):
    """systemctl --timestamp=unix gives @1794403638; empty when never."""
    v = (v or "").strip()
    if v.startswith("@"):
        try:
            return float(v[1:])
        except ValueError:
            return 0.0
    return 0.0


def usec_of(v):
    """LastTriggerUSec in unix form is also @epoch (seconds)."""
    return ts_of(v)


def when_of(v):
    """@epoch, or the dated form some timer properties keep despite --timestamp=unix
    ("Thu 2026-11-19 08:20:00 EST", local time); 0.0 when empty or unreadable."""
    v = (v or "").strip()
    if v.startswith("@"):
        return ts_of(v)
    parts = v.split()
    for i in range(len(parts) - 1):
        try:
            return datetime.datetime.strptime(parts[i] + " " + parts[i + 1], "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S").timestamp()
        except ValueError:
            continue
    return 0.0


SPAN_UNITS = {"us": 1e-6, "ms": 1e-3, "s": 1, "min": MIN, "h": H, "d": D, "w": 7 * D, "month": 30.44 * D, "y": 365.25 * D}


def span_of(v):
    """a systemd timespan ("10min 32.540477s") in seconds; None when empty, 0 or infinity"""
    v = (v or "").strip()
    if not v or v in ("0", "infinity"):
        return None
    total = 0.0
    for tok in v.split():
        num = tok.rstrip("abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz")
        unit = tok[len(num):] or "s"
        if unit not in SPAN_UNITS:
            return None
        try:
            total += float(num) * SPAN_UNITS[unit]
        except ValueError:
            return None
    return total


def next_run(ti):
    """when the timer fires next (epoch), 0.0 when unknown"""
    t = when_of(ti.get("NextElapseUSecRealtime"))
    if t:
        return t
    mono = span_of(ti.get("NextElapseUSecMonotonic"))
    if mono is not None and "SHELL_HEALTH_NOW" not in os.environ:
        return NOW + mono - time.clock_gettime(time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
    return 0.0


def due(t):
    """'in 3 min' / 'any moment' for an epoch in the future"""
    if not t:
        return ""
    left = t - NOW
    if left < 45:
        return "any moment"
    return "in " + span(left)


def last_wake():
    """when the laptop last started or woke from sleep (epoch); 0.0 when unknown"""
    if os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_WAKE"):
        try:
            return float(os.environ["SHELL_HEALTH_WAKE"])
        except ValueError:
            return 0.0
    boot = 0.0
    for line in read(os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_PROCSTAT") or "/proc/stat").splitlines():
        if line.startswith("btime "):
            try:
                boot = float(line.split()[1])
            except ValueError:
                pass
    # The journal is the record that holds: systemd garbage-collects sleep.target once it is inactive,
    # and the reloaded unit has no timestamps, so a wake read from it alone is lost after a few seconds
    # (2026-11-19: every job asleep through a suspend showed stale instead of healing).  The last
    # line a sleep service logs this boot is written as it finishes, that is, on resume.
    woke = 0.0
    rc, out = run(["journalctl", "-b", "-q", "--no-pager", "-o", "short-unix", "-n", "1"]
                  + [a for u in ("suspend", "hibernate", "hybrid-sleep", "suspend-then-hibernate")
                     for a in ("-u", "systemd-%s.service" % u)])
    if rc == 0 and out.strip():
        try:
            woke = float(out.strip().splitlines()[-1].split()[0])
        except ValueError:
            woke = 0.0
    if not woke:
        rc, out = run(["systemctl", "--timestamp=unix", "show", "-p", "InactiveEnterTimestamp", "sleep.target"])
        woke = ts_of(out.strip().partition("=")[2]) if rc == 0 else 0.0
    w = max(boot, woke)
    return w if w <= NOW else 0.0


def count(path):
    try:
        return int((read(path).strip() or "0").split()[0])
    except ValueError:
        return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data gathering
def systemd_show(units):
    props = "Id,LoadState,ActiveState,SubState,Result,ExecMainStatus,UnitFileState,NRestarts,ActiveEnterTimestamp,LastTriggerUSec,ExecMainExitTimestamp,NextElapseUSecRealtime,NextElapseUSecMonotonic"
    rc, out = run(SYSCTL + ["--timestamp=unix", "show", "-p", props] + units)
    if rc != 0 or not out.strip():
        return None                      # systemd did not answer (slow right after a wake): unknown
    info = {}
    for block in out.split("\n\n"):
        d = {}
        for line in block.splitlines():
            if "=" in line:
                k, v = line.split("=", 1)
                d[k] = v
        if d.get("Id"):
            info[d["Id"]] = d
    return info


def failed_units():
    rc, out = run(SYSCTL + ["list-units", "--failed", "--plain", "--no-legend", "--no-pager"])
    return [l.split()[0] for l in out.splitlines() if l.split()]


def gsettings(profile):
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env.pop("DCONF_PROFILE", None)
    if profile:
        env["DCONF_PROFILE"] = profile
    got = {}
    for key in ("last-backup", "periodic", "periodic-period"):
        rc, out = run(["gsettings", "get", "org.gnome.DejaDup", key], env=env)
        got[key] = out.strip().strip("'") if rc == 0 else None
    return got


def mounted(path):
    rc, out = run(["findmnt", "-n", "-o", "TARGET,FSTYPE", "-M", path], timeout=1.5)
    return rc == 0 and path in out


def listening(port):
    d = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_NETDIR") or "/proc/net"
    want = ":%04X" % port
    for name in ("tcp", "tcp6"):
        for line in read(os.path.join(d, name)).splitlines()[1:]:
            f = line.split()
            if len(f) > 3 and f[1].endswith(want) and f[3] == "0A":
                return True
    return False


def has_route():
    route = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_ROUTE") or "/proc/net/route"
    for line in read(route).splitlines()[1:]:
        f = line.split("\t") if "\t" in line else line.split()
        if len(f) > 3 and f[1] == "00000000" and int(f[3], 16) & 1:
            return True
    return False


def online():
    """Is the internet actually usable?  A default route alone is not enough: after a wake the route
    is back before DNS, and a captive portal (campus Wi-Fi) has a route but no internet.
    NetworkManager's own connectivity state (cached, no request) settles it; when NetworkManager
    cannot say ("unknown", or no nmcli), the route decides."""
    if not has_route():
        return False
    c = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_CONNECTIVITY")
    if c is None:
        rc, out = run(["nmcli", "-t", "networking", "connectivity"], timeout=1.0)
        c = out.strip() if rc == 0 else ""
    return c not in ("none", "portal", "limited")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- job table
BIN = HOME + "/.local/bin/"
MAIL_SCRIPTS = HOME + "/.emacs.d/scripts/"


def jrn(unit, n=80):
    return "journalctl --user -u %s -n %d --no-pager" % (unit, n)


def start(unit):
    return "systemctl --user start %s" % unit


def restart(unit):
    return "systemctl --user restart %s" % unit


TIMERS = [
    # id, name, timer, service, period, floor, state dir, bad_at, stale_at (streak), net, extra log
    dict(id="pull-mail", name="Mail sync", timer="pull-mail.timer", service="pull-mail.service",
         period=2 * MIN, floor=15 * MIN, streak="pull-mail", bad_at=2, net=True,
         repair=("pull-mail/davmail-restarted", "restarted DavMail itself")),
    dict(id="pull-calendars", name="Calendar sync", timer="pull-calendars.timer", service="pull-calendars.service",
         period=10 * MIN, floor=30 * MIN, streak="pull-calendars", bad_at=6, warn_at=3, net=True),
    dict(id="push-roam", name="Notes push to homeserver", timer="push-roam.timer", service="push-roam.service",
         period=10 * MIN, floor=30 * MIN, streak="push-roam", bad_at=2, net=True),
    dict(id="teams-refresh", name="Teams sign-in refresh", timer="teams-refresh.timer", service="teams-refresh.service",
         period=8 * H, net=True, log="journalctl --user -u teams-refresh.service -n 80 --no-pager"),
    dict(id="calibre-backup", name="Calibre database backup", timer="calibre-db-backup.timer",
         service="calibre-db-backup.service", period=7 * D, net=False,
         artifact=("glob", HOME + "/.local/share/calibre-db-backups", "metadata-", ".db"),
         log="tail -n 30 " + HOME + "/.local/share/calibre-db-backups/backup.log"),
    dict(id="matrix-backup", name="Matrix and Teams backup", timer="matrix-backup.timer",
         service="matrix-backup.service", period=7 * D, net=False,
         artifact=("dirs", HOME + "/backups/matrix", "", "")),
]

REASONS = {
    "davmail-down": "DavMail is not running (nothing on port 1143)",
    "microsoft-down": "Microsoft 365 itself is failing",
}


def mk(job, state, why, since=0.0, unit="", log="", run_cmd="", own_wake=False):
    """own_wake: the judge already knows when the trouble began and applied the wake grace itself"""
    return dict(id=job[0], name=job[1], state=state, since=iso(since), why=why, unit=unit,
                log=log, run=run_cmd, _net=job[2], _since=since, _own_wake=own_wake, _unknown="")


def judge_timer(t, info, wake=0.0):
    j = _judge_timer(t, info, wake)
    j["_own_wake"] = bool(t.get("streak"))       # its streak file dates the failures
    if t.get("repair"):
        note = repair_note(*t["repair"])
        if note:
            j["why"] += "; " + note
    return j


REPAIR_SHOWN = 6 * H


def repair_note(path, what):
    """A repair the job's script made by itself (a stamp file: epoch, then the retry's exit code),
    shown for a few hours so a fixed-itself problem is visible instead of silent."""
    lines = read(os.path.join(STATE, path)).split()
    try:
        when = float(lines[0])
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        return ""
    if NOW - when > REPAIR_SHOWN or when > NOW + 60:
        return ""
    res = lines[1] if len(lines) > 1 else ""
    return "%s %s%s" % (what, ago(NOW - when), ", which fixed it" if res == "0" else ", which did not help" if res else "")


def _judge_timer(t, info, wake=0.0):
    ti, si = info.get(t["timer"], {}), info.get(t["service"], {})
    ident = (t["id"], t["name"], t["net"])
    log = t.get("log") or jrn(t["service"])
    runc = start(t["service"])
    unit = t["timer"]
    if ti.get("LoadState", "not-found") == "not-found" or si.get("LoadState", "not-found") == "not-found":
        return mk(ident, "off", "not installed", unit=unit)
    if ti.get("ActiveState") != "active":
        if ti.get("UnitFileState") in ("disabled", "masked", "static", ""):
            return mk(ident, "off", "timer is switched off", unit=unit)
        return mk(ident, "failed", "its timer is not running", unit=unit, log=log, run_cmd=runc)

    # last success and the streak
    sdir = os.path.join(STATE, t["streak"]) if t.get("streak") else ""
    failures = count(sdir + "/failures") if sdir else 0
    reason = REASONS.get(read(sdir + "/reason").strip(), "") if sdir else ""
    last_run = mtime(sdir + "/failures") if sdir else 0.0
    since = 0.0
    if failures == 0 and sdir:
        since = last_run
    elif t.get("artifact"):
        since = artifact_time(t["artifact"])
    if not since:
        since = max(ts_of(si.get("ExecMainExitTimestamp")), 0.0) or usec_of(ti.get("LastTriggerUSec"))
    if t.get("artifact") and since == 0.0:
        since = artifact_time(t["artifact"])

    result = si.get("Result", "success")
    active = si.get("ActiveState")
    nxt = next_run(ti)
    running = active in ("active", "activating")
    # Failed only since the laptop woke a few minutes ago: Wi-Fi and DNS are still coming up
    # (2026-11-19: mail failed twice in the 3 minutes after a resume, then ran fine)
    if failures and t["net"] and wake and last_run >= wake - WAKE_SLACK and NOW - wake <= WAKE_GRACE:
        why = "%s since waking %s, while the network comes back; %s" % (
            "last run failed" if failures == 1 else "%d runs failed" % failures, ago(NOW - wake),
            "running again now" if running else "trying again " + (due(nxt) or "on its next run"))
        return mk(ident, "healing", why, since, unit, log, runc)
    if active == "failed" or (result not in ("success", "") and active not in ("active", "activating")):
        why = "the last run failed (exit %s)" % si.get("ExecMainStatus", "?")
        if failures:
            why = "%d runs in a row have failed" % failures
        return mk(ident, "failed", (reason + "; " if reason else "") + why, since, unit, log, runc)
    if failures >= t.get("bad_at", 99):
        return mk(ident, "failed", "%d runs in a row have failed%s" % (failures, "; " + reason if reason else ""),
                  since, unit, log, runc)
    if failures >= t.get("warn_at", 99):
        return mk(ident, "stale", "%d runs in a row have failed%s" % (failures, "; " + reason if reason else ""),
                  since, unit, log, runc)
    if failures and reason:
        return mk(ident, "stale", "last run failed; " + reason, since, unit, log, runc)

    if failures:
        left = t.get("warn_at", t.get("bad_at", 99)) - failures
        why = "%s failed; %s" % ("last run" if failures == 1 else "%d runs in a row" % failures,
                                  "running again now" if running else "trying again " + (due(nxt) or "on its next run"))
        if left > 0 and left < 90:
            why += " (%d more before it counts)" % left
        return mk(ident, "healing", why, since, unit, log, runc)

    period = t["period"]
    limit = max(3 * period, t.get("floor", 0)) if period < D else 2 * period + D
    # overdue by the clock, but the laptop was off or asleep for it: graded from the start or wake
    fresh = wake and wake > since and NOW - since > limit and NOW - wake <= limit
    if fresh or (not since and running):
        if running:
            why = "running now"
        else:
            why = "waiting for its first run since start-up or wake, due " + (due(nxt) or "soon")
        if since:
            why += "; last worked " + ago(NOW - since)
        return mk(ident, "healing", why, since, unit, log, runc)
    if not since:
        return mk(ident, "stale", "no completed run on record", 0.0, unit, log, runc)
    age = NOW - since
    if NOW - max(since, wake or 0.0) > limit:
        if wake and wake > since:
            why = "no run since start-up or wake %s; last worked %s, runs every %s" % (ago(NOW - wake), ago(NOW - since), span(period))
        else:
            why = "last worked %s, runs every %s" % (ago(age), span(period))
        if running:
            why += "; running now"
        return mk(ident, "stale", why, since, unit, log, runc)
    return mk(ident, "ok", ("ran " + ago(age)) if period < D else ("backed up " + ago(age)), since, unit, log, runc)


def artifact_time(spec):
    kind, d, pre, suf = spec
    best = 0.0
    try:
        for n in os.listdir(d):
            if kind == "glob" and not (n.startswith(pre) and n.endswith(suf)):
                continue
            if kind == "dirs" and not (len(n) == 10 and n[4] == "-" and n[7] == "-"):
                continue
            best = max(best, mtime(os.path.join(d, n)))
    except OSError:
        pass
    return best


def judge_service(ident, name, unit, info, net=False, log=None, run_cmd=None, extra=None, desktop_only=False):
    i = info.get(unit, {})
    ident = (ident, name, net)
    log = log or jrn(unit)
    run_cmd = run_cmd or restart(unit)
    if i.get("LoadState", "not-found") == "not-found":
        return mk(ident, "off", "not installed", unit=unit)
    act = i.get("ActiveState")
    since = ts_of(i.get("ActiveEnterTimestamp"))
    if act == "failed":
        st = i.get("ExecMainStatus", "?")
        why = "stopped with an error (exit %s)" % st
        if st == "78":
            why = "needs a full resync (run it by hand: onedrive --resync)"
        return mk(ident, "failed", why, since, unit, log, run_cmd)
    if act in ("inactive", "deactivating"):
        if i.get("UnitFileState") in ("disabled", "masked"):
            return mk(ident, "off", "switched off", unit=unit)
        if desktop_only and os.environ.get("XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP", "") != "Hyprland":
            return mk(ident, "off", "only runs under Hyprland", unit=unit)
        return mk(ident, "failed", "not running", since, unit, log, run_cmd)
    n = recent_restarts(ident[0], int(i.get("NRestarts") or 0))
    if act == "activating":
        return mk(ident, "healing" if n < 3 else "failed",
                  "starting or restarting (%s in the last hour)" % times(n), since, unit, log, run_cmd)
    if extra:
        r = extra(since)
        if r:
            state, why = r
            return mk(ident, state, why, since, unit, log, run_cmd)
    why = "running since " + ago(NOW - since).replace(" ago", "") if since else "running"
    if n:
        why += ", restarted %s in the last hour" % times(n)
    return mk(ident, "stale" if n >= RESTARTS_STALE else "ok", why, since or NOW, unit, log, run_cmd)


def times(n):
    return "once" if n == 1 else "%d times" % n


def recent_restarts(jid, total):
    """How many of the unit's NRestarts came in the last hour.  NRestarts only grows while the unit
    lives (OneDrive's twice-daily restart would read stale after a few days), so keep a short history
    of it in seen.json.  With no history yet, nothing is known to be recent: 0."""
    s = SEEN.setdefault("jobs", {}).setdefault(jid, {})
    hist = [h for h in s.get("restarts", []) if isinstance(h, list) and len(h) == 2 and NOW - h[0] <= 2 * RESTART_WINDOW]
    if hist and hist[-1][1] > total:
        hist = []                        # the counter went back: the unit was started afresh
    base = None
    for t, n in hist:
        if NOW - t >= RESTART_WINDOW:
            base = n                     # the newest sample at least an hour old
    if base is None:
        base = hist[0][1] if hist else total
    if not hist or hist[-1][1] != total or NOW - hist[-1][0] >= 10 * MIN:
        hist.append([NOW, total])
    s["restarts"] = hist[-40:]
    return max(0, total - base)


def judge_onedrive(info):
    j = judge_service("onedrive", "OneDrive sync", "onedrive.service", info, net=True)
    rt, rs = info.get("onedrive-restart.timer", {}), info.get("onedrive-restart.service", {})
    if j["state"] == "ok" and rt.get("LoadState") == "loaded":
        if rs.get("ActiveState") == "failed" or rs.get("Result") not in (None, "", "success"):
            j.update(state="failed", why="its twice-daily restart failed", log=jrn("onedrive-restart.service"),
                     run=restart("onedrive.service"))
        elif rt.get("ActiveState") != "active":
            j.update(state="stale", why="its restart timer is not running")
    return j


def judge_rclone(info):
    def mount_ok(since):
        if not mounted(os.path.join(RUNTIME, "Box")):
            if NOW - since < 60:
                return ("healing", "starting; the mount is not up yet")
            return ("failed", "running but the Box mount is gone")
        return None
    j = judge_service("rclone-box", "Box mount", "rclone-box.service", info, net=True, extra=mount_ok)
    if j["state"] == "ok":
        j["why"] = "mounted, up since " + ago(NOW - ts_of(info["rclone-box.service"].get("ActiveEnterTimestamp"))).replace(" ago", "")
    return j


def judge_davmail(info):
    def port(since):
        if not listening(1143):
            if NOW - since < 90:
                return ("healing", "starting; nothing on port 1143 yet")
            return ("failed", "running but nothing answers on port 1143")
        return None
    return judge_service("davmail", "DavMail", "davmail.service", info, net=True, extra=port)


def judge_matrix():
    """The local Matrix stack (~/Docker/matrix): Synapse and its bridges, by container health."""
    ident = ("matrix", "Matrix server and bridges", True)
    names = ["synapse", "mautrix-teams", "mautrix-gmessages"]
    log = "cd ~/Docker/matrix && docker compose logs --tail 80"
    runc = "cd ~/Docker/matrix && docker compose up -d"
    rc, out = run(["docker", "inspect", "-f", "{{.Name}} {{.State.Status}} {{if .State.Health}}{{.State.Health.Status}}{{else}}none{{end}} {{.State.StartedAt}}"] + names)
    rows = [l.split() for l in out.splitlines() if l.strip()]
    if rc == 124:
        j = mk(ident, "healing", "", 0.0, "", log, runc)
        j["_unknown"] = "Docker did not answer in time"
        return j
    if not rows:
        return mk(ident, "off", "not set up, or Docker is not running", unit="")
    seen = {r[0].lstrip("/"): r for r in rows if len(r) >= 3}
    bad, starting = [], []
    for n in names:
        r = seen.get(n)
        if r is None:
            if n == "synapse":
                bad.append(n + " missing")
            continue                      # a bridge that was never set up is not a failure
        if r[1] != "running" or r[2] == "unhealthy":
            bad.append("%s %s" % (n, r[1] if r[1] != "running" else "unhealthy"))
        elif r[2] == "starting":
            starting.append(n)
    if bad:
        return mk(ident, "failed", ", ".join(bad), 0.0, "", log, runc)
    if starting:
        return mk(ident, "healing", "starting: " + ", ".join(starting), 0.0, "", log, runc)
    return mk(ident, "ok", "%d containers healthy" % len(seen), NOW, "", log, runc)


def judge_archive():
    """The SD card that holds ~/Music (/mnt/archive, an automount).  It slips out in the bag; then mpd
    pins the dead filesystem and remounting says "File exists" (see the archive automount notes).
    Never touches the automount unless the card is there, so a missing card cannot hang the check."""
    ident = ("archive", "Music card (/mnt/archive)", False)
    dev = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_ARCHIVE_DEV") or "/dev/disk/by-label/archive"
    mp = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_ARCHIVE_DIR") or "/mnt/archive"
    log = "journalctl -u mnt-archive.mount -u mnt-archive.automount -n 40 --no-pager; findmnt " + mp
    runc = "systemctl --user restart mpd.service; sudo systemctl reset-failed mnt-archive.automount mnt-archive.mount; ls " + mp
    if not os.path.isdir(mp):
        return mk(ident, "off", "not set up here", unit="")
    if not os.path.exists(dev):
        return mk(ident, "stale", "the SD card is not detected; reseat it", 0.0, "", log, runc)
    rc, out = run(["stat", "-f", "-c", "%T", mp + "/"], timeout=1.5)
    if rc == 124:
        return mk(ident, "failed", "the card is in, but /mnt/archive does not answer (dead mount)", 0.0, "", log, runc)
    if rc != 0:
        return mk(ident, "failed", "the card is in, but /mnt/archive will not mount", 0.0, "", log, runc)
    return mk(ident, "ok", "mounted", NOW, "", log, runc)


def judge_dejadup(profiles):
    ident = ("dejadup", "Backup (Deja Dup)", False)
    log = "tail -n 40 " + HOME + "/.cache/deja-dup/duplicity.log"
    seen = [p for p in profiles if p["last-backup"] is not None]
    if not seen:
        return mk(ident, "off", "Deja Dup is not installed", unit="")
    if all(p["periodic"] == "false" for p in seen):
        return mk(ident, "off", "automatic backups are switched off", unit="", log=log)
    best = 0.0
    for p in seen:
        v = p["last-backup"]
        if v:
            try:
                best = max(best, datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(v.replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp())
            except ValueError:
                pass
    period = 7 * D
    for p in seen:
        try:
            period = max(1, int(p["periodic-period"])) * D
            break
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            pass
    runc = "deja-dup --backup"
    if not best:
        return mk(ident, "stale", "no finished backup on record", 0.0, "", log, runc)
    age = NOW - best
    limit = 2 * period + D if period >= D else 3 * period
    if age > limit:
        return mk(ident, "stale", "last backup %s, set to run every %d days" % (ago(age), period // D), best, "", log, runc)
    return mk(ident, "ok", "last backup " + ago(age), best, "", log, runc)


def judge_microsoft(wake=0.0):
    ident = ("microsoft", "Microsoft 365 link", True)
    path = os.path.join(STATE, "microsoft/health.json")
    log = MAIL_SCRIPTS + "ms-health status"
    runc = MAIL_SCRIPTS + "ms-health check"
    try:
        d = json.loads(read(path) or "{}")
    except ValueError:
        d = {}
    if not d:
        return mk(ident, "off", "no health record yet", unit="")
    st, detail = d.get("state", ""), d.get("detail", "")
    checked, since = float(d.get("checked") or 0), float(d.get("since") or 0)
    if st == "ok":
        return mk(ident, "ok", "answered " + ago(NOW - checked), checked, "", log, runc)
    if st == "offline":
        return mk(ident, "ok", "offline (Microsoft unreachable from here)", since, "", log, runc)
    if st == "auth":
        return mk(ident, "failed", "sign-in needed: run exchange-rules.py login", since, "", log, runc)
    # Down only since the laptop woke a few minutes ago: Wi-Fi and DNS are still coming up, the same
    # grace the timer jobs get (2026-11-20: the pill went red for a minute after every wake)
    if wake and since >= wake - WAKE_SLACK and NOW - wake <= WAKE_GRACE:
        return mk(ident, "healing", "no answer since waking %s, while the network comes back; checked again on the next sync%s"
                  % (ago(NOW - wake), " (" + detail + ")" if detail else ""), 0.0, "", log, runc, own_wake=True)
    return mk(ident, "failed", "Microsoft 365 is failing" + (": " + detail if detail else ""), since, "", log, runc, own_wake=True)


KNOWN = {t["service"] for t in TIMERS} | {t["timer"] for t in TIMERS} | {
    "davmail.service", "onedrive.service", "onedrive-restart.service", "onedrive-restart.timer",
    "rclone-box.service", "qs-socket-watch.service"}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run
def collect(cfg):
    units = []
    for t in TIMERS:
        units += [t["timer"], t["service"]]
    units += ["davmail.service", "onedrive.service", "onedrive-restart.timer", "onedrive-restart.service",
              "rclone-box.service", "qs-socket-watch.service", "mpd.service"]
    with cf.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as ex:
        f_show = ex.submit(systemd_show, units)
        f_failed = ex.submit(failed_units)
        f_def = ex.submit(gsettings, "")
        f_cos = ex.submit(gsettings, "/usr/share/dconf/profile/cosmic")
        f_wake = ex.submit(last_wake)
        try:
            info = f_show.result(timeout=2.6)
        except Exception:
            info = None
        unknown = "" if info is not None else "systemd did not answer in time"
        info = info or {}
        try:
            failed = f_failed.result(timeout=2.0)
        except Exception:
            failed = []
        try:
            wake = f_wake.result(timeout=2.0)
        except Exception:
            wake = 0.0
        profiles, gs_unknown = [], ""
        for f in (f_def, f_cos):
            try:
                profiles.append(f.result(timeout=2.0))
            except Exception:
                gs_unknown = "gsettings did not answer in time"
                profiles.append({"last-backup": None, "periodic": None, "periodic-period": None})
    jobs = [judge_timer(t, info, wake) for t in TIMERS]
    jobs.append(judge_davmail(info))
    jobs.append(judge_onedrive(info))
    jobs.append(judge_rclone(info))
    jobs.append(judge_dejadup(profiles))
    jobs.append(judge_microsoft(wake))
    jobs.append(judge_matrix())
    jobs.append(judge_service("qs-socket-watch", "Shell restart watchdog", "qs-socket-watch.service", info, desktop_only=True))
    jobs.append(judge_service("mpd", "Music player (mpd)", "mpd.service", info))
    jobs.append(judge_archive())
    if unknown:
        for j in jobs:
            if j["unit"].endswith((".service", ".timer")):
                j["_unknown"] = unknown
    if gs_unknown:
        for j in jobs:
            if j["id"] == "dejadup":
                j["_unknown"] = gs_unknown
    ignore = ignored_units(cfg)
    for u in failed:
        if u in KNOWN or any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(u, g) for g in ignore):
            continue
        # amber, not red: an unknown unit may not matter, and uwsm's fumon has already said it failed
        jobs.append(mk(("unit:" + u, u, False), "stale", "unit failed", unit=u, log=jrn(u),
                       run_cmd="systemctl --user reset-failed %s; systemctl --user restart %s" % (u, u)))
    return jobs, wake


# Failed units that are not worth a light, as fnmatch globs; health.json "ignoreUnits" adds to them.
IGNORE_UNITS = [
    "dbus-:*",              # D-Bus activation attempts (a second notification daemon asked for the name)
    "desktop-test.service",  # the test run that sends its own notification when it is red
]


def ignored_units(cfg):
    return IGNORE_UNITS + list(cfg.get("ignoreUnits", []))


def seen_path():
    return os.path.join(STATE, "shell-health/seen.json")


def load_seen():
    try:
        seen = json.loads(read(seen_path()) or "{}")
    except ValueError:
        seen = {}
    return seen if isinstance(seen, dict) else {}


def apply_memory_and_offline(jobs, seen, wake=0.0):
    """Everything that needs memory across runs, in order:
    1. unknown (a probe timed out): the last known state, saying so, never a quiet "off" or green;
    2. offline: network jobs get GRACE before they count;
    3. a network job that went bad only since a wake gets WAKE_GRACE (judges that date their own
       failures, own_wake, already did this better);
    4. confirmation: bad for less than CONFIRM is healing, "checking again"."""
    on = online()
    if on:
        seen.pop("offline_since", None)
    elif not seen.get("offline_since"):
        seen["offline_since"] = NOW
    off_for = NOW - seen["offline_since"] if not on else 0
    for j in jobs:
        s = seen.setdefault("jobs", {}).setdefault(j["id"], {})
        if j["_unknown"]:
            last = s.get("last")
            if isinstance(last, dict) and last.get("state") in ("ok", "healing", "stale", "failed", "off"):
                j["state"] = last["state"]
                j["why"] = "could not check just now (%s); last known: %s" % (j["_unknown"], last.get("why", ""))
            else:
                j["state"] = "healing"
                j["why"] = "could not check yet (%s); trying again" % j["_unknown"]
            if s.get("ok") and j["state"] != "ok":
                j["since"] = iso(s["ok"])
            continue
        raw = j["state"]
        # bad_since: when the job last stopped being ok.  Healing counts too, so a grace period that
        # ends in a real failure raises it at once instead of starting the confirmation over.
        if raw in ("ok", "off"):
            s.pop("bad_since", None)
        elif not s.get("bad_since"):
            s["bad_since"] = NOW
        s["last"] = {"state": raw, "why": j["why"]}
        if j["state"] == "ok" and j["_since"]:
            s["ok"] = max(s.get("ok", 0), j["_since"])
        elif j["state"] == "ok":
            s["ok"] = NOW
        if not j["since"] and s.get("ok") and j["state"] in ("stale", "failed", "healing"):
            j["since"] = iso(s["ok"])
        if not on and j["_net"]:
            if j["state"] in ("stale", "failed", "healing"):
                if off_for < GRACE:
                    j["state"] = "healing"
                    j["why"] = "offline for %s; will try again once back online (%s)" % (span(off_for), j["why"])
                else:
                    j["why"] = "offline for %s; %s" % (span(off_for), j["why"])
            elif j["state"] == "ok" and "offline" not in j["why"]:
                j["why"] += " (offline now)"
        bad_since = s.get("bad_since") or NOW
        if (j["state"] in ("stale", "failed") and j["_net"] and not j["_own_wake"] and wake
                and bad_since >= wake - WAKE_SLACK and NOW - wake <= WAKE_GRACE):
            j["state"] = "healing"
            j["why"] = "since waking %s, while the network comes back (%s)" % (ago(NOW - wake), j["why"])
        if j["state"] in ("stale", "failed") and NOW - bad_since < CONFIRM:
            j["state"] = "healing"
            j["why"] = "just went wrong, checking again before raising it (%s)" % j["why"]
    return seen


def save_seen(seen):
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(seen_path()), exist_ok=True)
        tmp = seen_path() + ".tmp"
        with open(tmp, "w") as f:
            json.dump(seen, f)
        os.replace(tmp, seen_path())
    except OSError:
        pass


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- notices and settings
CFG_DEFAULT = dict(updatesNag=50, staleListDays=14, diskPercent=10, diskGB=5, espMB=20, hidden=[], ignoreUnits=[],
                   notices=dict(updates=True, firmware=True, disk=True, reboot=True))


def load_config():
    cfg = json.loads(json.dumps(CFG_DEFAULT))
    path = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_CONFIG") or os.path.join(HOME, ".config/shell/health.json")
    try:
        d = json.loads(read(path) or "{}")
    except ValueError:
        d = {}
    if not isinstance(d, dict):
        return cfg
    for k in ("updatesNag", "staleListDays", "diskPercent", "diskGB", "espMB"):
        if isinstance(d.get(k), (int, float)) and not isinstance(d.get(k), bool) and d[k] >= 0:
            cfg[k] = d[k]
    if isinstance(d.get("hidden"), list):
        cfg["hidden"] = [str(x) for x in d["hidden"]]
    if isinstance(d.get("ignoreUnits"), list):
        cfg["ignoreUnits"] = [str(x) for x in d["ignoreUnits"]]
    if isinstance(d.get("notices"), dict):
        for k in cfg["notices"]:
            if isinstance(d["notices"].get(k), bool):
                cfg["notices"][k] = d["notices"][k]
    return cfg


DISK_FSTYPES = {"ext2", "ext3", "ext4", "xfs", "btrfs", "f2fs", "vfat", "exfat", "ntfs", "ntfs3", "zfs", "jfs", "reiserfs"}
DISK_PREFIXES = ("/mnt/", "/media/", "/run/media/")
DISK_FIXED = {"/", "/home", "/boot", "/boot/efi"}
ESP = ("/boot/efi", "/boot")


def unescape(p):
    out, i = [], 0
    while i < len(p):
        if p[i] == "\\" and i + 3 < len(p) and p[i + 1:i + 4].isdigit():
            out.append(chr(int(p[i + 1:i + 4], 8)))
            i += 4
        else:
            out.append(p[i])
            i += 1
    return "".join(out)


def mounts():
    """[(mountpoint, fstype, total, free)] for the filesystems worth a disk warning."""
    table = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_DISKS")
    found = []
    if table:
        try:
            d = json.loads(read(table) or "{}")
        except ValueError:
            d = {}
        for mp, v in d.items():
            found.append((mp, v.get("fstype", ""), v.get("dev", mp), v.get("total", 0), v.get("free", 0)))
    else:
        for line in read("/proc/self/mountinfo").splitlines():
            f = line.split()
            if len(f) < 10 or "-" not in f:
                continue
            k = f.index("-")
            mp, fstype, dev = unescape(f[4]), f[k + 1], f[2]
            if fstype not in DISK_FSTYPES:
                continue
            if not (mp in DISK_FIXED or mp.startswith(DISK_PREFIXES)):
                continue
            try:
                st = os.statvfs(mp)
            except OSError:
                continue
            found.append((mp, fstype, dev, st.f_blocks * st.f_frsize, st.f_bavail * st.f_frsize))
    out, devs = [], set()
    for mp, fstype, dev, total, free in found:
        if fstype not in DISK_FSTYPES or not (mp in DISK_FIXED or mp.startswith(DISK_PREFIXES)):
            continue
        if dev in devs or total <= 0:
            continue
        devs.add(dev)
        out.append((mp, fstype, total, free))
    return out


def gb(b):
    return "%.1f GB" % (b / 1e9) if b >= 1e9 else "%d MB" % round(b / 1e6)


def disk_notices(cfg):
    rows = []
    for mp, fstype, total, free in mounts():
        pct = 100.0 * free / total
        if mp in ESP:
            low = free < cfg["espMB"] * 1e6
        else:
            low = pct < cfg["diskPercent"] or free < cfg["diskGB"] * 1e9
        if not low:
            continue
        why = "%s free of %s (%d%%)" % (gb(free), gb(total), round(pct))
        rows.append(notice("disk:" + mp, "Low disk space: " + mp, why, "disk", cmd="df -h %s; du -xh --max-depth=2 %s 2>/dev/null | sort -h | tail -15" % (mp, mp),
                           count=1, actionable=True, say=True))
    return rows


def notice(id_, name, why, group, cmd="", count=0, actionable=False, say=False):
    return dict(id=id_, name=name, state="notice", since="", why=why, unit="", log="", run="", kind="notice",
                group=group, count=count, detail=why, cmd=cmd, actionable=actionable, say=say)


def updates_program():
    p = os.environ.get("SHELL_HEALTH_UPDATES")
    if p == "none":
        return None
    if p:
        return p
    for c in (os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "updates-check"), BIN + "updates-check"):
        if os.path.isfile(c):
            return c
    return None


def update_notices(cfg, refresh):
    prog = updates_program()
    if not prog:
        return []
    rc, out = run([sys.executable, "-I", prog, "--refresh" if refresh else "--cached"], timeout=25 if refresh else 2.0)
    try:
        rows = json.loads(out).get("rows", [])
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        return []
    res = []
    for r in rows:
        i, n = r.get("id"), int(r.get("count") or 0)
        if i == "apt":
            nag = cfg["updatesNag"]
            lists = r.get("listsAgeDays")
            act = bool(r.get("security")) or n > nag or (lists is not None and lists >= cfg["staleListDays"])
            if n or act:
                res.append(notice("apt", "Package updates", r.get("detail", ""), "updates", r.get("cmd", ""), n, act))
        elif i == "flatpak" and n:
            res.append(notice("flatpak", "Flatpak updates", r.get("detail", ""), "updates", r.get("cmd", ""), n))
        elif i == "firmware" and n:
            res.append(notice("firmware", "Firmware updates", r.get("detail", ""), "firmware", r.get("cmd", ""), n))
        elif i == "reboot":
            res.append(notice("reboot", "Restart needed", r.get("detail", ""), "reboot", r.get("cmd", ""), 1, True, True))
    return res


def notices_for(cfg, refresh=False):
    rows = []
    if cfg["notices"]["disk"]:
        rows += disk_notices(cfg)
    ups = update_notices(cfg, refresh) if any(cfg["notices"][k] for k in ("updates", "firmware", "reboot")) else []
    rows += [r for r in ups if cfg["notices"].get(r["group"], True)]
    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (not r["actionable"],))
    return rows


def worst_of(jobs):
    rank = {"ok": 0, "stale": 1, "failed": 2}
    w = "ok"
    for j in jobs:
        if j["state"] in rank and rank[j["state"]] > rank[w]:
            w = j["state"]
    return w


def main(argv):
    mode, only, refresh = "json", None, False
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a == "--json":
            mode = "json"
        elif a == "--text":
            mode = "text"
        elif a == "--refresh":
            refresh = True
        elif a == "--only" and i + 1 < len(argv):
            only = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
        else:
            print("usage: shell-health [--json|--text] [--only ID] [--refresh]", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        i += 1
    cfg = load_config()
    global SEEN
    SEEN = load_seen()
    jobs, wake = collect(cfg)
    seen = apply_memory_and_offline(jobs, SEEN, wake)
    save_seen(seen)
    order = {"failed": 0, "stale": 1, "healing": 2, "ok": 3, "off": 4}
    jobs.sort(key=lambda j: order[j["state"]])
    notes = notices_for(cfg, refresh)
    everything = [{k: v for k, v in j.items() if not k.startswith("_")} for j in jobs] + notes
    hidden = [{"id": j["id"], "name": j["name"]} for j in everything if j["id"] in cfg["hidden"]]
    out = [j for j in everything if j["id"] not in cfg["hidden"]]
    if only:
        out = [j for j in out if j["id"] == only]
    worst = worst_of([j for j in out if j["state"] != "notice"])
    attention = sum(1 for j in out if j["state"] == "notice" and j["actionable"])
    if mode == "json":
        print(json.dumps({"worst": worst, "attention": attention, "hidden": hidden, "jobs": out}, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    print("worst: %s" % worst)
    for j in out:
        if j["state"] == "notice":
            print("%-7s %-16s %-26s %s%s" % ("NOTICE", j["id"], j["name"], j["why"], "  [worth a look]" if j["actionable"] else ""))
            continue
        last = ago(NOW - datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(j["since"]).timestamp()) if j["since"] else "-"
        print("%-7s %-16s %-26s %s  [last ok: %s]" % (j["state"].upper(), j["id"], j["name"], j["why"], last))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
